{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional}
{album: Traditional Ballads}
{meta: language English}
{key: Am}
{meta: tags ballad, traditional}
{chord_style: trailing}
{copyright: Traditional English ballad. Public domain.}

{start_of_verse}
Are you going to Scarborough Fair [Am] [G] [Am]
Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme [C] [Am] [C] [D] [Am]
Remember me to one who lives there [Am] [C] [G] [Am]
She once was a true love of mine [Am] [G] [Am]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Tell her to make me a cambric shirt [Am] [G] [Am]
Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme [C] [Am] [C] [D] [Am]
Without no seams nor needlework [Am] [C] [G] [Am]
Then she'll be a true love of mine [Am] [G] [Am]
{end_of_verse}
